From 56fa1cb5a67d443ddcee4d5436eeca746a8c525a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooja Jagadeesh Doijode <pdoijode@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 5 Mar 2024 10:03:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: [GR] Premature EOR sent after GR

In a scaled setup, because the peer's subgroup packet queue was full,
BGP was unable to generate UPDATE messages for all the L2VPN NLRIs
and encode them into packets. Because of this, BGP thought there were
no further packets to send, and sent EOR prematurely.

On GR helper, since EOR was received before all the routes could be
refreshed, stale paths were deleted and added back once the restarting
node advertised those paths again. This resulted in traffic loss after
GR.

Signed-off-by: Pooja Jagadeesh Doijode <pdoijode@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit cd1d953b97472edf3febc8cedea8ff9696463b6c)
Signed-off-by: Anant Kishor Sharma <anant.kishor-sharma@hpe.com>
---
 bgpd/bgp_packet.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_packet.c b/bgpd/bgp_packet.c
index e5b7e8e05..5ecada8d1 100644
--- a/bgpd/bgp_packet.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_packet.c
@@ -580,11 +580,10 @@ void bgp_generate_updgrp_packets(struct event *thread)
 				 *   general, and thus the practice is
 				 *   recommended.
 				 */
-				if (!(PAF_SUBGRP(paf))->t_coalesce &&
-				    peer->afc_nego[afi][safi] &&
+				if (!(PAF_SUBGRP(paf))->t_coalesce && peer->afc_nego[afi][safi] &&
 				    peer->synctime &&
-				    !CHECK_FLAG(peer->af_sflags[afi][safi],
-						PEER_STATUS_EOR_SEND)) {
+				    !CHECK_FLAG(peer->af_sflags[afi][safi], PEER_STATUS_EOR_SEND) &&
+				    advertise_list_is_empty(PAF_SUBGRP(paf))) {
 					/* If EOR is disabled, the message is
 					 * not sent.
 					 */
